Context: T145, plan 004 item O5 by operator decision 2026-11-19 (ADR 0014). Design choices: the capability indication rides as the first request frame after the unchanged hello (V offer, v welcome) instead of extending the hello frame, because an old hub's strict readers would either misframe trailing hello bytes as the next request (silent corruption) or refuse the auth frame with CodeAuth, which is indistinguishable from a refused credential; the unknown-marker refusal arrives as CodeMalformed, so a bad credential still costs one round trip and an old hub costs one refused connection per process (capsOff, same lifetime rule as the unsupported workspace exchange). ProtocolVersion stays 1 - strict equality forbids a version-bump negotiation path. The hub accepts Z on any connection (no per-connection capability state); its defense is per-frame: rawLen must fit the plain record section maximum (64 MiB + 12 B per record given the validated count), compLen must fit the batch bound, and DecodeAll runs with WithDecodeAllCapLimit so a zstd bomb cannot allocate past the declared length (klauspost v1.20.0 exposes the option; the too-small declared length surfaces as ErrDecoderSizeExceeded, mapped to CodeTooLarge). Encoder and decoder are lazily created process singletons (sync.OnceValue) so the hub pays no encoder pool and the device pays no decoder; EncodeAll/DecodeAll are concurrency-safe. Plain fallback when compression does not win keeps the wire marker honest; probes are always plain. State machine: encoding only - tla/Sync.tla unchanged, reasoning recorded in ADR 0014 and tla/README.md. Verification: make check green, FuzzReadFrame 30 s (1.8 M execs) clean with compressed and caps seeds, cmd/ohya e2e (serve, join, remote MCP over a local relay) green on the negotiated-compressed path, TestOldHubFallsBackToPlainFrames pins the mixed-version fallback both directions.
